<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Natchez chiefdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1200 CE – 1731 CE (approx.) · capital Grand Village of the Natchez</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Mississippian-style chiefdom of the Lower Mississippi, ruled by the sacred Great Sun until its war with the French in 1729.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Natchez descended from the Plaquemine culture of the Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> Valley. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerald-mound">Emerald Mound</a>, one of the largest platform mounds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, was built from around 1250, and by the late 17th century the political centre was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-village-of-the-natchez">Grand Village</a> on St Catherine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, near the modern city of Natchez, Mississippi.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-sun">Great Sun</a>, a sacred ruler said to descend from the sun, lived on a mound facing a temple where an eternal fire burned. Society was divided into Suns, Nobles, Honoured People and commoners, and members of the upper ranks had to marry commoners, so rank shifted through the female line. When the war chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tattooed-serpent">Tattooed Serpent</a> died in 1725, wives and retainers were killed to accompany him, as described by the French settler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antoine-simon-le-page-du-pratz">Le Page du Pratz</a>. The Natchez farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and spoke a language isolate.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-louisiana">French Louisiana</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-rosalie">Fort Rosalie</a> in 1716. In 1729 the Natchez attacked it, killing around 230 colonists. French and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/choctaw-nation">Choctaw</a> forces retaliated, and by 1731 hundreds of Natchez, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-sun">Great Sun</a>, had been sold into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a>. Survivors joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chickasaw-nation">Chickasaw</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Muscogee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherokee">Cherokee</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1200 CE – 1731 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">North America and Oceania</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.58%;width:10.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1200 CE – 1731 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Grand Village of the Natchez</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tattooed Serpent</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Natchez traditional religion, sun cult</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Natchez</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Natchez, Great Sun's chiefdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1466&amp;focus=natchez-chiefdom" aria-label="Natchez chiefdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2323 1030 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Natchez chiefdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2643 1286L2659 1339"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2659 1339h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2643 1286h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2643 1286h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Grand Village of the Natchez. <a href="/atlas?year=1466&amp;focus=natchez-chiefdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

